selector_to_html = {"a[href=\"VoluteSection.html#pyskyfire.ducts.volute_section.VoluteSection\"]": "<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"pyskyfire.ducts.volute_section.VoluteSection\">\n<span class=\"property\"><span class=\"k\"><span class=\"pre\">class</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span></span><span class=\"sig-prename descclassname\"><span class=\"pre\">pyskyfire.ducts.volute_section.</span></span><span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">VoluteSection</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">inlet_width</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">aspect_ratio</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">1.0</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">max_aspect_ratio</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">None</span></span></em><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span></dt><dd><p>Bases: <a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3/library/abc.html#abc.ABC\" title=\"(in Python v3.15)\"><code class=\"xref py py-obj docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">abc.ABC</span></code></a></p><p>A volute cross-section family with a fixed inlet slot width.</p><p>Subclasses define a shape parameterised by a positive <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">size</span></code> and an\n<code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">aspect</span></code>. All methods accept a scalar or a one-dimensional array of\nsizes, and return matching arrays; <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">aspect</span></code> defaults to the family\u2019s own\n<code class=\"xref py py-attr docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">aspect_ratio</span></code> where it is not given.</p></dd>", "a[href=\"../../common/section_geometry/index.html#module-pyskyfire.common.section_geometry\"]": "<h1 class=\"tippy-header\" style=\"margin-top: 0;\">pyskyfire.common.section_geometry<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#module-pyskyfire.common.section_geometry\" title=\"Link to this heading\">\u00b6</a></h1><p>Planar arc geometry used by section analytics and physical construction.</p>", "a[href=\"#module-contents\"]": "<h2 class=\"tippy-header\" style=\"margin-top: 0;\">Module Contents<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#module-contents\" title=\"Link to this heading\">\u00b6</a></h2>", "a[href=\"../../common/rotation/index.html#pyskyfire.common.rotation.rotation_sign\"]": "<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"pyskyfire.common.rotation.rotation_sign\">\n<span class=\"sig-prename descclassname\"><span class=\"pre\">pyskyfire.common.rotation.</span></span><span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">rotation_sign</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">value</span></span></em><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span> <span class=\"sig-return\"><span class=\"sig-return-icon\">\u2192</span> <span class=\"sig-return-typehint\"><a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3/builtins/functions.html#float\" title=\"(in Python v3.15)\"><span class=\"pre\">float</span></a></span></span></dt><dd><p><code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">+1.0</span></code> for a counterclockwise sense, <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">-1.0</span></code> for a clockwise one.</p></dd>", "a[href=\"../../regen/cross_section/ChannelSection.html#pyskyfire.regen.cross_section.ChannelSection\"]": "<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"pyskyfire.regen.cross_section.ChannelSection\">\n<span class=\"property\"><span class=\"k\"><span class=\"pre\">class</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span></span><span class=\"sig-prename descclassname\"><span class=\"pre\">pyskyfire.regen.cross_section.</span></span><span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">ChannelSection</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">n_points</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">16</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"keyword-only-separator o\"><abbr title=\"Keyword-only parameters separator (PEP 3102)\"><span class=\"pre\">*</span></abbr></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">exposure</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">None</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">exposure_angles</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">None</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">enable_fin</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">False</span></span></em><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span></dt><dd><p>A section with floor, roof, and two sidewalls.</p><p>exposure maps surface names to centred fractions in [0, 1], optionally\ndesign-input callables. Unspecified surfaces are inactive; the default is\nthe complete floor. exposure_angles selects rounded-lobe spans in radians\ninstead. A surface cannot specify both forms.</p><p>enable_fin applies one symmetric rib model to both sidewalls, incompatible\nwith direct sidewall exposure. CoolingCircuit supplies its own fin switch;\nindependent sections use this switch. All surfaces count toward Dh.</p></dd>", "a[href=\"#pyskyfire.ducts.volute_section.solve_section_size\"]": "<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"pyskyfire.ducts.volute_section.solve_section_size\">\n<span class=\"sig-prename descclassname\"><span class=\"pre\">pyskyfire.ducts.volute_section.</span></span><span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">solve_section_size</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">section</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">residual</span></span></em><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span></dt><dd><p>The smallest section of a family satisfying an area law.</p><p>Works down three regimes as the law asks for less and less area, and is\nshared by every passage that sizes a section this way \u2013 a volute closing\non its tongue and a manifold closing on its dead point face the same\nproblem, because both laws want zero area somewhere no section can deliver.</p><p>Away from that point the design aspect ratio can hold the law, and only the\nsize is solved for. Closer in, the law wants less area than even the\nsmallest section at that aspect: the passage can never be narrower than the\nopening feeding it, so the size has bottomed out. Flattening is the way past\nthat \u2013 holding the size at its floor and stretching the section across the\nopening shrinks its area without narrowing the passage \u2013 so the aspect\nratio is solved for instead, up to the family\u2019s limit. Only when the\nflattest allowed section is still too big does the law get clipped, and it\nis clipped to that flattest section rather than to the design-aspect one,\nwhich is as close to the law as the family can get.</p></dd>", "a[href=\"EllipticalSlottedSection.html#pyskyfire.ducts.volute_section.EllipticalSlottedSection\"]": "<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"pyskyfire.ducts.volute_section.EllipticalSlottedSection\">\n<span class=\"property\"><span class=\"k\"><span class=\"pre\">class</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span></span><span class=\"sig-prename descclassname\"><span class=\"pre\">pyskyfire.ducts.volute_section.</span></span><span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">EllipticalSlottedSection</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">inlet_width</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">fillet_radius</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">throat_length</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">0.0</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">aspect_ratio</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">1.0</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">max_aspect_ratio</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">4.0</span></span></em><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span></dt><dd><p>Bases: <code class=\"xref py py-obj docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">VoluteSection</span></code></p><p>An elliptical bore opening into a parallel-sided inlet slot.</p><p>This is the cast pump-volute shape: an elliptical passage fed through a\nslot of fixed width <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">inlet_width</span></code>, with the junction between each slot\nwall and the bore rounded by a fillet of user-set radius. At the default\naspect ratio of one the ellipse is a circle, which is the common case.</p><p class=\"rubric\">Notes</p><p><code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">size</span></code> is the semi-axis across the slot, so it plays exactly the role the\nbore radius does for a circle and the slot still fixes its floor at\n<code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">inlet_width</span> <span class=\"pre\">/</span> <span class=\"pre\">2</span></code>. Writing <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">c</span></code> for it, <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">a</span> <span class=\"pre\">=</span> <span class=\"pre\">c</span> <span class=\"pre\">/</span> <span class=\"pre\">aspect</span></code> for the\nsemi-axis outward from the inlet plane, <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">b</span></code> for the inlet width, <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">r_f</span></code>\nfor the fillet radius and <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">L</span></code> for the throat length, each fillet is\nplaced by requiring it to be tangent to its slot wall and to the bore.</p><p>The fillets round a <em>reflex</em> corner \u2013 the passage opens outward as it\nleaves the slot \u2013 so each fillet centre sits outside the passage at\n<code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">v</span> <span class=\"pre\">=</span> <span class=\"pre\">+/-</span> <span class=\"pre\">(b/2</span> <span class=\"pre\">+</span> <span class=\"pre\">r_f)</span></code> and touches the bore externally. Writing the\ntangency point as the ellipse parameter <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">t</span></code> and the ellipse\u2019s outward\nunit normal there as <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">n(t)</span></code>, the fillet centre is <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">E(t)</span> <span class=\"pre\">+</span> <span class=\"pre\">r_f*n(t)</span></code>,\nand requiring its <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">v</span></code> to equal <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">-(b/2</span> <span class=\"pre\">+</span> <span class=\"pre\">r_f)</span></code> fixes <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">t</span></code> alone:</p></dd>", "a[href=\"#module-pyskyfire.ducts.volute_section\"]": "<h1 class=\"tippy-header\" style=\"margin-top: 0;\">pyskyfire.ducts.volute_section<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#module-pyskyfire.ducts.volute_section\" title=\"Link to this heading\">\u00b6</a></h1><p>Volute cross-section families.</p><p>A volute cross-section is a closed planar region measured in a section plane\nthat contains the machine axis. Its two coordinates are</p>", "a[href=\"#functions\"]": "<h2 class=\"tippy-header\" style=\"margin-top: 0;\">Functions<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#functions\" title=\"Link to this heading\">\u00b6</a></h2>", "a[href=\"#classes\"]": "<h2 class=\"tippy-header\" style=\"margin-top: 0;\">Classes<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#classes\" title=\"Link to this heading\">\u00b6</a></h2>", "a[href=\"#pyskyfire.ducts.volute_section.section_frames\"]": "<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"pyskyfire.ducts.volute_section.section_frames\">\n<span class=\"sig-prename descclassname\"><span class=\"pre\">pyskyfire.ducts.volute_section.</span></span><span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">section_frames</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">theta</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"keyword-only-separator o\"><abbr title=\"Keyword-only parameters separator (PEP 3102)\"><span class=\"pre\">*</span></abbr></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">tilt</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">0.0</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">sign</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">1.0</span></span></em><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span></dt><dd><p>Bases of the section planes at one or more azimuths about <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">+z</span></code>.</p><p>A section lies in the plane through the machine axis at its azimuth, so the\n<code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">(u,</span> <span class=\"pre\">v)</span></code> coordinates it is measured in map to a radial and an axial\ndirection there, rotated together by <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">tilt</span></code>.</p><p><code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">sign</span></code> is the rotation sense from\n<a class=\"reference internal\" href=\"../../common/rotation/index.html#pyskyfire.common.rotation.rotation_sign\" title=\"pyskyfire.common.rotation.rotation_sign\"><code class=\"xref py py-func docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">rotation_sign()</span></code></a>: <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">+1</span></code> winds\ncounterclockwise about <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">+z</span></code> as azimuth increases, <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">-1</span></code> clockwise. It\nmirrors where each section sits without touching the section\u2019s own shape,\nsince the mirror plane contains the axis and so maps every section plane to\nanother one.</p><p><code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">tilt</span></code> stays absolute under that mirror: which axial way a discharge\npoints is a packaging choice independent of which way the machine spins.</p></dd>"}
skip_classes = ["headerlink", "sd-stretched-link"]

window.onload = function () {
    for (const [select, tip_html] of Object.entries(selector_to_html)) {
        const links = document.querySelectorAll(` ${select}`);
        for (const link of links) {
            if (skip_classes.some(c => link.classList.contains(c))) {
                continue;
            }

            tippy(link, {
                content: tip_html,
                allowHTML: true,
                arrow: true,
                placement: 'auto-start', maxWidth: 600, interactive: false,
                onShow(instance) {MathJax.typesetPromise([instance.popper]).then(() => {});},
            });
        };
    };
    console.log("tippy tips loaded!");
};
